Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the mysql module
==========================================

The native MySQL/MariaDB DBI driver belongs to qore-mysql-module. HTML API
reference and upstream example tests belong to qore-mysql-module-doc.
Debhelper creates matching detached debug symbols.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native build environment containing the packaged Qore runtime
and libqore-dev, then install Build-Depends from debian/control. The current
qualification target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages.
Other releases and architectures need a matching SDK and native qualification.
Cross builds are rejected because Qore executes during the build.

Packages use distribution MariaDB Connector/C (LGPL), via libmariadb-dev-compat.
No client library is bundled. Runtime dependencies include libmariadb3 but no
database server or client tools. MySQL server interoperability needs separate
integration qualification; the package tests use MariaDB.

The build preserves distribution hardening flags. Native Qore modules resolve
Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore. debian/rules derives minimum
runtime and libqore SONAME dependencies from the installed SDK; dh_shlibdeps
supplies other shared libraries. The runtime package is not Multi-Arch: same
because it requires the native Qore interpreter. This module has no AOT user
modules or compiler metadata; ordinary dh_strip is appropriate.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

The +ds source excludes m4/acx_pthread.m4, an unused legacy Autoconf macro with
no accompanying license notice. The upstream checkout retains this file; the
repacked source supports the CMake build. Other embedded license notices are
recorded in debian/copyright, including the historical TiddlyWiki manual.

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot precedes version
2.2. From a clean committed checkout:

    version=2.2~git20260928.1+ds
    mkdir -p ../mysql-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-mysql-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' ':!m4/acx_pthread.m4' | xz > \
        "../mysql-package-work/qore-mysql-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../mysql-package-work/qore-mysql-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../mysql-package-work
    cp -a debian "../mysql-package-work/qore-mysql-module-$version/"
    cd "../mysql-package-work/qore-mysql-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x into a clean directory. With dependencies
preinstalled, build as an unprivileged user with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) do not need Doxygen. Architecture-independent
builds (-A) produce documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc suppress documentation; the profile also omits the doc
package. Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

Build and installed tests initialize a disposable MariaDB server under a
private temporary directory and connect through its Unix socket. TCP is disabled;
no host database, account or credentials are used. Passwordless root access is
limited to this private socket, and the server/data are removed on exit.
LOCAL INFILE is enabled to exercise the driver's guarded native bulk loader.
A connection preflight prevents silent success from missing database settings.

All three upstream suites cover DBI data types, columnar results, transactions,
prepared statements, error details, deadlocks and native bulk loading. Installed
tests copy fixtures away from checkout/build paths. A fresh qcc executable
performs a parameterized database round trip using only the installed driver.
The MariaDB build must also load with Qore's --lgpl option.

Check source/binary Lintian, debug symbols, hardening, installation without the
SDK or server, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and
reproducibility from different build directories and parallelism settings.
Retain source/package hashes, dependency versions, audit and test logs.
Testing PPA publication is separate from approval for a final general release.
